 | yes | 20 | 73 | 113 | 114\\nNAMD\\nMolecular Dynamics\\nDesigned for high-performance simulation of large molecular systems\\nVERSION\\n3.1.a3\\nACCELERATED FEATURES\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openmm/openmm/issues/2971\",\n      \"title\": \"A100, V100 and multi-gpu benchmarks · Issue #2971 · openmm ...\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"A100, V100 and multi-gpu benchmarks · Issue #2971 · openmm ...\\nMy motivation was mainly to figure out how to speed up very large to huge systems, or at least figure out what performance to expect: after I saw my system running at 0.4 ns/day I got into benchmarking :) The performance for large systems on single GPUs here is scaling almost linearly with memory bandwidth (T4 = 320 GB/s, V100 = 900 GB/s and\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"warnings\": null,\n  \"metadata\": null,\n  \"session_id\": \"ses_eb36ab900ffesPzhYt7ZPkYvbn\"\n}","metadata":{"provider":"parallel","truncated":false},"title":"Parallel Web Search: GROMACS performance ns/day A100 H100 benchmark small system 30000 atoms","time":{"start":1792286257767,"end":1792286258452}},"id":"prt_14c95f17b001bZJIjskIyKlb2F","sessionID":"ses_eb36ab900ffesPzhYt7ZPkYvbn","messageID":"msg_14c954a75001y9PBT0C9lqkWAt"}}
