viding unrivalled fire safety, environmental protection, increased\\nasset performance and real cost savings.\\nMIDEL 7131 is a synthetic ester dielectric fluid designed to provide an\\nalternative to mineral oil, silicone fluid and dry-type transformers.\\nMIDEL 7131 has a high fire point, significantly increasing the fire safety of your\\nMIDEL offers more than the benefits of a fire-safe fluid – there are also\\nclear advantages to be gained in cost and risk reductions, deployment\\ninnovations, corporate social responsibility, and asset performance.\\nMIDEL 7131 is the only synthetic ester approved by both FM Global\\nand UL.\\nMIDEL\\n®\\nSAFETY INSIDE\\nMIDEL 7131 is supplied in accordance with IEC industry standard acceptance values and test methods. The displayed typical values do not form part of this specification.\\nIEC 61099\\nMIDEL 7131\\nProperty\\nTest Method\\nUn-used new fluid\\nproperty requirements\\nTypical Values\\nPhysical\\nColour\\nISO 2211\\nMax. 200 Hazen\\n125\\nAppearance\\nClear, free from water and suspended\\nmatter and sediment\\nClear, free from water and suspended\\nmatter and sediment\\nDensity at 20˚C (kg/dm 3 )\\nISO 3675 or ISO 12185\\nMax. 1\\n0.97\\nKinematic Viscosity (mm 2 /sec)\\nISO 3104\\nat 40°C\\nMax. 35\\n29\\nat -20°C\\nMax. 3000\\n1440\\nFlash Point PMCC (°C)\\nISO 2719\\nMin. 250\\n260\\nFire Point (°C)\\nISO 2592\\nMin. 300\\n316\\nPour Point (°C)\\nISO 3016\\nMax. -45\\n-56\\nCrystallization\\nIEC 61099 (2010 Annex A)\\nNo crystals\\nNo crystals\\nBiodegradation\\nReadily Biodegradable\\nReadily Biodegradable\\nElectrical\\nDielectric Breakdown (kV)\\nIEC 60156\\nMin. 45\\n75\\nPower Factor at 90°C\\nIEC 60247\\nMax. 0.03\\n<0.008\\nDC Resistivity at 90°C (G Ω .m)\\nIEC 60247\\nMin. 2\\n20\\nChemical\\nWater Content (mg/kg)\\nIEC 60814\\nMax. 200\\n50\\nAcidity (mg KOH/g)\\nIEC 62021-1 or IEC 62021-2\\nMax. 0.03\\n<0.03\\nOxidation Stability (164hr)\\nIEC 61125C\\nTotal Acidity (mg KOH/g)\\nMax. 0.3\\n0.02\\nTotal Sludge (% mass)\\nMax. 0.01\\n<0.01\\nMIDEL 7131\\nProtecting lives, the environment and property since the 1970s\\nDeveloped in the 1970s, MIDEL 7131 is today used in\\nthousands of new transformers to increase safety. Over the\\nsame period, MIDEL 7131 has gained an excellent reputation\\nas a cost effective retrofill fluid for the replacement of\\nflammable mineral oil.\\nINCREASED FIRE SAFETY\\n• 100% fire safety record\\n• High fire point (>300°C) – K class classification\\n• K3 classification (IEC 61039)\\nof breakdown voltage (up to 600ppm)\\n• Allows moisture to migrate from cellulose into the fluid,\\nthus extending cellulose life\\n• Very high saturation limit (2,700 ppm @ 20 ˚ C)\\nmaking precipitation of free water virtually impossible\\nSYNTHETIC ESTER ADVANTAGES\\n• Superior oxygen stability\\n• Flexible - used in non free-breathing and breathing systems\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/1142213\",\n      \"title\": \"Pre-breakdown currents in insulating liquids stressed with ...\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Sandia National Laboratoires, P.O.Box 5800, Albuquerque, NM 87185, USA\\nAbstract- This paper is aimed at investigation of the pre-\\nbreakdown conduction characteristics of insulating liquids. Two\\nmineral oils and a synthetic ester fluid were used in the tests.\\nThe current-voltage characteristics have been measured in the\\nDC breakdown voltages have been\\nmonitored and registered. It has been shown that MIDEL 7131\\nsynthetic ester has a lower breakdown strength as compared\\nwith the tested mineral oils. Also it has been shown that positive\\nbreakdown voltage is lower than the negative breakdown voltage\\nfor the insulating liquids used in this study.\\nIndex\\ninsulating oil (Shell Ltd) and Midel 7131 synthetic ester\\nliquid (Midel Ltd). This choice is determined by widespread\\nuse of the transformer oil and the Diala D oil in power\\napplications and pulsed power systems. Midel 7131 liquid is a\\nrelatively new dielectric fluid which is beginning to be used\\nas a low-toxicity alternative to the mineral insulating oils.\\nDiala D oil is a commercially available insulating oil which\\nis used as a transformer insulating liquid. It is a blend of\\nhighly refined mineral oils and an aromatic extract from a\\ndistillate. Midel 7131 is a synthetic ester based insulating\\nfluid which is used mostly in transformers and other electrical\\nequipment. Midel 7131 has excellent fire resistance properties\\nand is classified as a non-toxic fluid [1].\\nThe dielectric properties of Midel 7131 and Diala D\\ninsulating liquids have been studied previously. Static\\ndielectric permitivities of Diala D and MIDEL 7131 liquids\\nare  2.2 [3] and  3.2 [1] respectively. It has been shown that\\nthe value of the DC Ohmic conductivity of the Midel 7131\\nliquid at room temperature slightly is higher than the values\\nof the DC conductivity for the Diala D oil. Also it was shown\\nthat the MIDEL 7131 liquid has a lower breakdown strength\\n1.2/50  s impulses\\nand 17-20% lower AC breakdown\\nvoltage. However the technical data sheet for Midel 7131\\nstates that its minimum AC breakdown voltage of this liquid\\nis slightly higher that the breakdown voltage of an unnamed\\nmineral oil [5].\\nIn order to analyse the breakdown behavior of the dielectric\\n- 32 kV\\nExperiments show a clear difference in dielectric behavior\\nof the mineral oils and the ester fluid. For the positively\\nstressed needle electrode the breakdown voltages for all three\\nliquids are in the range between 18-20 kV, the difference\\nbetween the breakdown voltages for the MIDEL 7131 fluid\\nand the mineral oils is relatively small.\\nHowever, this\\n25.4  m\\nsituation changes for the negatively stressed needle. Mineral\\ntransformer oils (Grosvenor Oil Services and Diala D) were\\nable to withstand negative voltages up to 35 kV without\\nbreakdown. In contrast, the electric breakdown in the Midel\\n7131 ester liquid was observed at 32 kV for negatively\\nstressed needle electrode.\\n5\\n10\\n15\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13073820\",\n      \"title\": \"Oil-Based Phase Change Emulsions Endowed with High Thermal Conductivity and Responsive Rheological Behavior\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2026-03-27\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"To overcome the low thermal conductivity and flow channel clogging inherent in traditional phase change materials (PCMs) for immersion cooling, this study develops a novel oil-based phase change emulsion (PCE) integrating high thermal transport with adaptive rheological behavior.\\nA liquid thermal conductivity enhancer was synthesized by modifying epoxidized soybean oil with LiTFSI and blending it with a synthetic ester to form a dielectric base fluid. A mid-to-low-temperature PCM (Span65) was then incorporated via surfactant-free ultrasonic emulsification.\\nThe resulting PCE exhibits a tunable phase-change window (25~40 °C) driven by interfacial confinement effects and a multiscale lamellar network. It achieves significantly enhanced thermal conductivity (15% increase over base oil) while maintaining excellent electrical insulation (<10^−9 S/cm).\\nIn contrast, mineral oil– and silicone oil–based systems, despite their comparatively lower thermal conductivity, offer inherent electrical insulation, chemical stability, and non-corrosive behavior [15].\\nCurrently, immersion cooling dielectrics primarily encompass mineral oils [16], silicone oils [17], vegetable oils [18], nanofluids [19,20,21,22], and synthetic ester-based oils [23,24,25].\\nSubsequently, by incorporating this modified TCE into a synthetic ester-based base fluid, we achieved an optimal balance between viscosity and thermal conductivity.\\nThis study presents a multifunctional phase-change coolant (EF6 + Span65), integrating a modified oil-soluble thermally conductive enhancer (EF6) with Span65. The system achieves synergistic enhancement of thermal management performance while preserving high electrical insulation (σ < 10^−9 S cm^−1) and thermal stability.\\nKey features include: (i) linearly enhanced thermal conductivity with increasing EF6 content; (ii) precise tuning of the phase change window to 25~40 °C—ideal for immersion cooling of Li-ion batteries and high-power electronics; (iii) gradient, multi-stage latent heat absorption/release over a broad temperature range, boosting thermal buffering\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.shell.us/business/fuels-and-lubricants/lubricants-for-business/products/midel/_jcr_content/root/main/section_895034773/promo_copy/links/item0.stream/1761247250447/c47738ab43da61ac90016c2b8619b92ec0ef48b8/midel-7131-product-brochure.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"Synthetic Ester Transformer Liquid Product Brochure\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2025-09-26\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Shell MIDEL 7131 is a synthetic ester dielectric liquid. An alternative to conventional mineral oil and silicone fluid filled transformers, it is deployed in a wide range of distribution and power transformers, including transformers over 400 kV. 6\\nCompared to conventional mineral oil and silicone liquid, Shell MIDEL 7131 can:\\n• maintain its dielectric\\nproperties at much higher moisture contents (up to 600 ppm at 20˚C) • dissolve more water\\nto potentially slow cellulose aging • avoid the risk of\\ncondensation associated with water in conventional mineral oil.\\nCold weather protection 6\\nThey are also active in ASTM, IEEE, IEC and CIGRÉ working groups, and regularly undertake extensive projects with industrial associations and academic bodies. This depth of experience means that the Shell MIDEL team is able to provide an exceptional level of technical support and guidance.\\nShell MIDEL 7131 fluid properties\\nProperties Method ASTM D8240 IEC 61099 Shell MIDEL 7131 (typical values) 9\\nColor (Hazen units) ISO 2211 D2129\\nMax. 200 Max. 200 125\\nAppearance Visual Bright and clear Clear, free from water, suspended matter and sediment\\nClear, free from water, suspended matter and sediment\\nDensity (kg/dm 3 ) ISO 3675 D1298/D4052\\nMax. 1.00 @15°C Max.\\n1,000 @20°C 0.97\\nKinematic viscosity @100°C (mm 2 /s)\\nD445 Max. 10 5.3\\nKinematic viscosity @40°C (mm 2 /s)\\nISO 3104 D445\\nMax. 35 Max. 35 29\\nKinematic viscosity @−20°C (mm 2 /s)\\nISO 3104 D445\\nMax. 3,000 Max. 3,000 1,440\\nFlash point (°C) ISO 2719 D92\\nMin. 250 Min. 250 260\\nFire point (°C) ISO 2592 D92\\nMin. 300 Min. 300 316\\nPour point (°C) ISO 3016 D97\\nMax. −45 Max. −45 −56\\nBiodegradability 2 (%) OECD 301 Readily biodegradable\\nBreakdown voltage (kV) IEC 60156 Min. 45 > 75\\nBreakdown voltage 1 mm (kV) D1816 20 41\\nBreakdown voltage 2 mm (kV) D1816 35 58\\nImpulse breakdown (kV) D3300 110 134\\nWater content (bulk) (mg/kg) IEC 60814 D1533\\nMax. 200 Max. 200 50\\nDielectric dissipation factor @ 90°C and 50Hz (%)\\nIEC 60247 Max. 0.03 0.027\\nDielectric dissipation factor @ 25°C and 60Hz (%)\\nD924 Max. 0.1 0.043\\nDielectric dissipation factor @100°C and 60Hz (%)\\nD924 Max. 3.0 1.77\\nPCB content (mg/kg) D4059 Not detectable Not detectable\\nAcidity/neutralization value (mg KOH/g)\\nIEC 62021-1 D974\\nMax. 0.03 Max.\\n0.03 < 0.03\\nOxidation stability (164 hrs) – total acidity (mg KOH/g)\\nIEC 61125C Max. 0.3 Max. 0.3 0.02\\nOxidation stability (164 hrs) – sludge (% mass)\\nIEC 61125C Max. 0.02 Max. 0.01 < 0.01\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.castrol.com/content/dam/castrol/country-sites-new/en_gb/united-kingdom/home/documents/products/castrol-on-immersion-cooling-fluid-dc-15-product-data.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"ON Immersion Cooling Fluid DC 15 | Castrol\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2023-10-26\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Product Data\\nON Immersion Cooling Fluid DC 15\\nImmersion Cooling Fluid\\nDescription\\nCastrol ON Immersion Cooling Fluid DC 15 is a synthetic hydrocarbon based dielectric coolant.\\nApplication\\nImmersion Cooling Fluid DC 15 is a single phase coolant designed for use in electrical/electronic cooling systems. It has excellent flow properties and thermal properties. This product also provides a superior oxidative stability, excellent dielectric properties, low temperature properties and excellent hydrolytic stability.\\nAdvantages\\nLow viscosity fluid providing excellent flow properties . Excellent thermal properties. Superior oxidative stability, low temperature properties and excellent hydrolytic stability. Excellent dielectric properties. Compatible with most commercially available elastomers. Zero Global Warming Potential (GWP) cooling solution.\\nPage: 1/2\\nTypical Characteristics\\nName Method Units DC 15\\nDensity @ 15.6°C / 60°F ISO 12185 / ASTM D4052 kg/m³ 835\\nKinematic Viscosity @ 100°C / 212°F ISO 3104 / ASTM D445 mm²/s 2.2\\nKinematic Viscosity @ 40°C / 104°F ISO 3104 / ASTM D445 mm²/s 7.5\\nKinematic Viscosity @ 20°C / 104°F ISO 3104 / ASTM D445 mm²/s 14.7\\nKinematic Viscosity @ 0°C / 104°F ISO 3104 / ASTM D445 mm²/s 35.9\\nPour Point ISO 3016 / ASTM D97 °C/°F -41 / -42\\nFlash Point - PMCC ISO 2719 / ASTM D93 °C/°F 154 / 309\\nFlash Point - COC ISO 2592 / ASTM D92 °C/°F 166 / 330\\nBreakdown Voltage IEC 60156 kV > 25\\nDielectric strength IEC 60156 kV / mm > 10\\nElectrical conductivity @ 25°C / 77°F DIN EN ISO 60247 mod. Flucon Epsilon pS/m < 50\\nDielectric constant (permittivity @ 25°C / 77°F)\\nDIN EN ISO 60247 mod. Flucon Epsilon - 2.09\\nSpecific Heat @ 40°C / 104°F ASTM E1269 kJ/kg.K 2.24\\nThermal conductivity @ 40°C / 104°F ASTM D7896 W/m.K 0.126\\nParticle Count (at filling point) ISO 4406 - 15/12/09\\nAppearance clear & bright\\nColour (ASTM) ASTM D1500 - < 0.5\\nON Immersion Cooling Fluid DC 15 22 Aug 2023 Castrol, the Castrol logo and related marks are trademarks of Castrol Limited, used under licence.\\nThis data sheet and the information it contains is believed to be accurate as of the date of printing. However, no warranty or representation, express or implied, is made as to its accuracy or completeness.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.shell.com/business-customers/lubricants-for-business/sector-expertise/power-industry/wind-power/shell-midel-transformer-oils-for-wind/_jcr_content/root/main/section/promo/links/item0.stream/1756741832357/506b6d14ec95fa48b8d8ed8c27b98d1c67571fad/midel-wind-brochure-v8.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"Shell MIDEL 7131 Synthetic ester transformer liquid brochure\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2025-08-15\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"July 2025\\nSynthetic ester transformer liquid\\nFire-safe 1 and readily biodegradable 2\\nSafety inside\\nShell MIDEL 7131 is a synthetic ester dielectric liquid – an alternative to conventional mineral oil and silicone fluid filled transformers. First used in the 1970s, 3 Shell MIDEL 7131 is used worldwide. 4\\n1 The fire point of conventional mineral oil in transformers is approximately 170°C, whereas with Shell MIDEL 7131 it is in excess of 300°C. Shell MIDEL’s fire safety may lead to a reduction in the requirements for additional fire protection. 5\\nFilling a system with Shell MIDEL 7131 instead of conventional mineral oil increases its fire safety because Shell MIDEL 7131 has a much higher fire point (> 300°C) and a 100% fire safety record.\\nIf the transformer fails to withstand the corrosive atmosphere, it will need to undergo expensive unplanned maintenance – specifying a fluid such as Shell MIDEL that is oxygen stable and proven to work means greater assurance for operators. 4,6\\nIncreased fire safety\\n• K Class high fire point\\n(> 300°C) to IEC 61039 1\\n• 100% fire safety record 4\\n• Suitable for installation within a\\nturbine • FM Approved and UL listed\\ntransformer fluid\\nHigh performance\\n• Conducive to lower levels of\\nmaintenance • High-temperature performance\\nfacilitates compact transformer designs • Greater moisture tolerance\\nthan conventional mineral oil, silicone liquid and natural ester 6\\n• Lower no-load losses than cast-\\nresin transformers, reducing energy consumption in low-wind conditions 4\\nGreater environmental protection\\n• Readily biodegradable\\naccording to OECD 301 2\\n• Non-hazardous 2\\nShell MIDEL 7131 fluid properties\\nProperty Test method IEC 61099 unused new fluid property requirements Shell MIDEL 7131 typical values\\nPhysical\\nColour (Hazen) ISO 2211 Max. 200 125\\nAppearance Clear, free from water, suspended matter and sediment\\nClear, free from water, suspended matter and sediment\\nDensity at 20°C (kg/dm 3 ) ISO 3675 or ISO 12185\\nMax. 1 0.97\\nKinematic viscosity (mm 2 /s) ISO 3104\\n@40°C Max. 35 29\\n@-20°C Max. 3,000 1,440\\nFlash point, PMCC (°C) ISO 2719 Min. 250 260\\nFire point (°C) ISO 2592 Min. 300 316\\nPour point (°C) ISO 3016 Max. −45 −56\\nCrystallisation IEC 61099 (2010 Annex A)\\nNo crystals No crystals\\nBiodegradation 2 OECD 301 B, C, F Readily biodegradable Readily biodegradable\\nElectrical\\nDielectric breakdown (kV) IEC 60156 Min. 45 > 75\\nPower factor at 90°C IEC 60247 Max. 0.03 < 0.008\\nDC resistivity at 90°C (GΩ·m)\\nIEC 60247 Min. 2 > 20\\nChemical\\nWater content (mg/kg) IEC 60814 Max. 200 50\\nAcidity (mg KOH/g) IEC 62021-1 or EC 62021-2\\nMax. 0.03 < 0.03\\nOxidation stability (164 h) IEC 61125C\\nTotal acidity (mg KOH/g) Max. 0.3 0.02\\nTotal sludge (% mass) Max. 0.01 < 0.01\\nReferences\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.shell.us/business/fuels-and-lubricants/lubricants-for-business/sector-expertise/power-industry/wind/shell-midel-transformer-oils-for-wind/_jcr_content/root/main/section/promo/links/item0.stream/1758143638463/2f02fb818f58f7674494b1db46736489a7851e91/shell-midel-7131-seventeen-sep-2025.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"Synthetic Ester Transformer Liquid Product Brochure\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2025-08-29\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Shell MIDEL 7131 is a synthetic ester dielectric liquid. An alternative to conventional mineral oil and silicone fluid filled transformers, it is deployed in a wide range of distribution and power transformers, including transformers over 400 kV. 6\\nFirst used in the 1970s, 7 Shell MIDEL 7131 is used worldwide in new transformers, and in existing transformers as a retrofill fluid to replace conventional mineral oil.\\nFire safety 1\\n40\\n50\\n60\\n0 1,000\\nMoisture content (ppm)\\n400 500 100 300 200\\n70\\n80\\n90\\nShell MIDEL 7131\\nSilicone liquid\\nConventional mineral oil\\n0 600 700 800 900\\nEffect of moisture on breakdown voltage at 20°C (IEC 60156, 2.5 mm).\\nA graph showing the effect of moisture on breakdown voltage of Shell MIDEL 7131, conventional mineral oil and silicone liquid, with breakdown voltage on the y-axis and moisture content on the x-axis, as fully described in the text.\\nVery high moisture saturation limit (2,700 ppm at 20˚C), which makes precipitation of free water virtually impossible.\\nCompared to conventional mineral oil and silicone liquid, Shell MIDEL 7131 can:\\n• maintain its dielectric\\nproperties at much higher moisture contents (up to 600 ppm at 20˚C) • dissolve more water\\nto potentially slow cellulose aging • avoid the risk of\\ncondensation associated with water in conventional mineral oil.\\nCold weather protection 6\\nThey are also active in ASTM, IEEE, IEC and CIGRÉ working groups, and regularly undertake extensive projects with industrial associations and academic bodies. This depth of experience means that the Shell MIDEL team is able to provide an exceptional level of technical support and guidance.\\nShell MIDEL 7131 fluid properties\\nProperty Test method IEC 61099 unused new fluid property requirements Shell MIDEL 7131 typical values 9\\nPhysical\\nColor (Hazen) ISO 2211 Max. 200 125\\nAppearance Clear, free from water, suspended matter and sediment\\nClear, free from water, suspended matter and sediment\\nDensity at 20°C (kg/dm 3 ) ISO 3675 or ISO 12185\\nMax. 1 0.97\\nKinematic viscosity (mm 2 /s) ISO 3104\\n@40°C Max. 35 29\\n@ −20°C Max. 3,000 1,440\\nFlash point, PMCC (°C) ISO 2719 Min. 250 260\\nFire point (°C) ISO 2592 Min. 300 316\\nPour point (°C) ISO 3016 Max. −45 −56\\nCrystallization IEC 61099 (2010 Annex A)\\nNo crystals No crystals\\nBiodegradation 2 OECD 301 B, C, F Readily biodegradable Readily biodegradable\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.thebusinessresearchcompany.com/report/immersion-cooling-fluids-global-market-report\",\n      \"title\": \"Immersion Cooling Fluids Market Size Forecast Report 2026-2030\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Immersion cooling fluids refer to specially engineered dielectric liquids used to thermally manage electronic and electrical equipment by fully or partially submerging components directly in the fluid. They are used to provide uniform cooling, reduce energy consumption, eliminate the need for traditional air-based cooling, and improve reliability and lifespan of electronic equipment. The main technologies for immersion cooling fluids are single-phase immersion cooling and two-phase immersion cooling. Single-phase immersion cooling refers to a technique for cooling electrical components that involve totally submerging the apparatus in a single-phase dielectric heat transfer fluid that is either passively cycled by the heated coolant's natural convection or actively circulated by a pump. The cooling fluid includes mineral oil, synthetic fluids, fluorocarbon-based fluids, and other cooling fluids. The various applications involve high-performance computing, edge computing, cryptocurrency mining, artificial intelligence, and other applications and are used in transformers, data centers, EV batteries, and solar photovoltaics.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nyco-group.com/ester/coolant-fluid\",\n      \"title\": \"Coolant fluids\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Coolant fluids\\nNYCO synthetic esters enhance fire safety and thermal conductivity while offering an ultra-low viscosity solution for improved cooling efficiency.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"warnings\": null,\n  \"metadata\": null,\n  \"session_id\": \"ses_eb36ab900ffesPzhYt7ZPkYvbn\"\n}","metadata":{"provider":"parallel","truncated":false},"title":"Parallel Web Search: single-phase immersion cooling dielectric fluid mineral oil synthetic ester viscosity thermal conductivity Midel","time":{"start":1792286258023,"end":1792286258710}},"id":"prt_14c95f299001p9TJFHmYzIkATG","sessionID":"ses_eb36ab900ffesPzhYt7ZPkYvbn","messageID":"msg_14c954a75001y9PBT0C9lqkWAt"}}
